<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore mid-distillate stocks corrected-TDB.</title>
<headline>Singapore mid-distillate stocks corrected-TDB.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's middle distillate stocks for the week May 29-June 4 totalled 10.243 million barrels, the Trade Development Board said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>The TDB said in a statement received by Reuter that the figure was corrected from the originally reported 1.9 billion barrels.</p>
<p>&quot;We would like to inform you that there is a typo error (in one of our sources of data),&quot; the TDB said.</p>
<p>The latest data indicates that middle distillate stocks fell 301,000 barrels from the week before.</p>
<p>Middle distillate stocks include gas oil and kerosene.</p>
<p>The data is reported by the TDB each Thursday.  </p>
<p>Last Thursday the TDB also reported that light distillate stocks rose in the week ended June 4 by 94,000 barrels to 6.756 million barrels and residues fell 465,000 barrels to 10.312 million.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65 870 3082)</p>
